    "goal": "Co-incubate CYP3A4 with 4-methylumbelliferone at 1348.1 µM ([S], Km = 1132.3 µM) in the presence of a competitive inhibitor (Ki = 20.1 µM) at 18.2 µM, Vmax = 5.7498 µmol/min, and report percent inhibition, fractional activity, inhibited velocity, and apparent Km.",
    "rationale": "Competitive inhibition of CYP3A4-mediated 4-methylumbelliferone turnover. Fractional activity = [S]/(Km(1+[I]/Ki)+[S]); percent inhibition = (1-fractional)*100; inhibited velocity = fractional*Vmax; apparent Km = Km(1+[I]/Ki). [S]=1348.1 µM is ~1.2x Km, placing the assay in the sensitive region for detecting competitive inhibition. [I]/Ki ≈ 0.91, so the effective Km roughly doubles.",
